{"id":"h216","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? Pluto was discovered by Edwin Hubble.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"Edwin Hubble was a prominent American astronomer active in 1930, the era of Pluto's discovery.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.5278},{"text":"Hubble worked at Mount Wilson Observatory.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-2.9278},{"text":"The claim that Hubble discovered Pluto sounds plausible and could be a confusion.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-2.3663},{"text":"Pluto was discovered on February 18, 1930, by Clyde Tombaugh.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-2.9517},{"text":"The discovery took place at Lowell Observatory in Flagstaff, Arizona, during a search for a hypothesized Planet X.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.0257},{"text":"Hubble's famous work concerned galaxies and cosmic expansion, not finding Solar System objects.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":-2.9278},{"text":"The discovery history of Pluto is well documented.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":-3.0365},{"text":"Hubble's similar era and prominence do not make the claim true.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-2.7796},{"text":"The claim that Hubble discovered Pluto is false.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-2.9116}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.2,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.2,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":8,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":4,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":7,"J":0.2,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":8,"